Sorting is the process of arranging data (like numbers, strings, or objects) 
in a specific sequence, typically ascending or descending.

Core Goal
To transform disorganized data into a structured order, making searching, retrieval,
analysis, and processing significantly faster and more efficient.

Time complexity typically ranges from O(n \log n) for efficient algorithms like 
merge sort to O(n^2) for basic ones, while space complexity varies between O(1) and O(n).
